-- title:
--   Weight at most p+1 for a curve's mod p eigensystem
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime with $p \neq 2$, and let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $\mathbb{Z}$ with $\Delta_W \neq 0$ whose mod $p$ representation is irreducible in the sense of `ModRepIsIrreducible`: the $p$-torsion subgroup of the points of $W$ base-changed to $\mathbb{Q}$ and then to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is nontrivial, and every Galois-stable $\mathbb{Z}/p$-submodule of it is $\bot$ or $\top$. Let $N'$ be a nonzero natural number with $p \nmid N'$, and assume that if $p = 3$ then $N'$ has a prime factor $q$ with $q \equiv 2 \pmod 3$. Let $S_0$ be a finite set of natural numbers with $p \in S_0$, let $k \in \mathbb{Z}$ with $k \geq 2$, and let $\mathfrak{m}_k$ be a maximal ideal of `heckeAlgebra N' k S₀`, the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of the space of cusp forms of weight $k$ for $\Gamma_0(N')$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N'$ outside $S_0$ together with the operators $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N'$ outside $S_0$. Assume $p \in \mathfrak{m}_k$ and that for every prime $\ell \notin S_0$ with $\ell \nmid N'$ and $\ell \nmid \Delta_W$ one has $T_\ell - a_\ell(W) \in \mathfrak{m}_k$, where $a_\ell(W) = \ell + 1 - \#W(\mathbb{Z}/\ell)$ is the trace of Frobenius of the reduction of $W$ modulo $\ell$. Then there exist an integer $k'$ with $2 \leq k' \leq p+1$, a natural number $i$, and a maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}'$ of `heckeAlgebra N' k' S₀` containing $p$ such that $T_\ell - \ell^{i} a_\ell(W) \in \mathfrak{m}'$ for all primes $\ell \notin S_0$ with $\ell \nmid N'$ and $\ell \nmid \Delta_W$.
--
--   This is the weight part of Serre's conjecture in Edixhoven's formulation, specialised to the mod $p$ Hecke eigensystem attached to an elliptic curve: the level $N'$ is unchanged and the weight is brought into the range $[2, p+1]$ at the cost of a twist by a power of the mod $p$ cyclotomic character, recorded here as the factor $\ell^{i}$ in the eigenvalue congruences. It feeds the construction of a newform of the required level in [`WeierstrassCurve.isResiduallyModularOfLevel_div_of_isNewform_of_inertia_moves_torsion_of_two_dvd_of_eq_three`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.isResiduallyModularOfLevel_div_of_isNewform_of_inertia_moves_torsion_of_two_dvd_of_eq_three).
